\f1\fs22 \'93A cabinet meeting on a Sunday morning, your Serene Corporateness?\'94 the Director of Moral Observance complained as he crabbed his corpulent butt into a chair at the board table. The chair creaked, despite its lofty brand, high design values and sturdy construction. \'93I\'92m expected at church.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93\'85 where you expect to be lauded and fed,\'94 Dunhilton rejoined.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Even so, CEO, Sunday is a day for quiet reflection on charts and numbers, and to give thanks that wealth accrues to those virtuous enough to deserve it,\'94 Moral Observance ventured.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Well, perhaps church should not be on the morning after Saturday night,\'94 Dunhilton baited. \'93If you could focus your attentions on preventing lewd thoughts of\'97oh I dunno, sedition\'85\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Moral Observance blanched and belched. His morning\'92s breakfast degustation wasn\'92t agreeing with him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Attempted murder,\'94 Dunhilton went on slowly, extracting the greatest unease from Moral Observance. \'93gate-crashing a private church service\'97a Holy Joint Venture, no less\'97crimes against music\'85 If you could have clamped down on just one of these social ills, I might not be calling a cabinet meeting during church hours.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, your Serene Corporateness.\'94 Moral Observance tried to look abashed, but his eyes intransigently trailed towards the plate of tantalising pastries on the board table. They were just far enough out of his reach; if he wanted one he\'92d need to make to make a indecorous lunge for the plate.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton surveyed the directors present. Behind their grim smiles he could see them rehearsing their craven, self-interested proposals in their heads; he\'92d heard them all before. Corrections wanted fresh criminals for private prisons. Housing salivated over dense Ghetto redevelopment. Tourism wanted his Elvi World theme park. Defence wanted to conscript them for Indonesian palm oil fantasies. These were all excellent ideas, the CEO conceded, which together could in the fullness of time yield a fully integrated master plan of synergistic opportunities going forward. He just hated the idea of any of these grunts profiting from any of it. \'93Now. The Elvi,\'94 he said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93ELVIS: Putting the slave back in slavery,\'94 Tourism quoted wistfully. \'93Grayling knew how to market.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I still wonder why we ever emancipated them,\'94 Housing muttered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Moral Observance spoke through the crumbs on his lips. \'93It\'92s apparent the Elvi pay no regard for the one true religion. I doubt any of them know the meaning of a balance sheet or a profit statement. And I am most concerned by this Holy-Momma-worship the Elvi are indulging in.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry diplomatically coughed, and glanced at the CEO. Neither wanted to discuss their virus project in a wider cabinet meeting. \'93There are intelligence efforts currently in progress regarding the Holy Momma.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I trust you have the initiatives well in hand, Gerry,\'94 Dunhilton prompted.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Indeed, CEO, I have,\'94 Gerry answered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'94Very well.\'94 Dunhilton cut off Moral Observance\'92s objections with a raised hand. \'93You\'92ve all been briefed on the St Hedges incursion\'97parachutes, aircraft, the Air Force\'92s\'85\'94 he paused meaningfully, \'93\'85difficulties. Defence will be providing a full written report by end of day.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Defence seemed to collapse from the inside out, like a deflating airbed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93But the parachute assault was merely delivery,\'94 Dunhilton continued. He stabbed his tablet with his middle finger, which fired up the conference room holo screen. \'93Can anyone tell me how this guy thinks he can upstage the Very Arch Business Bishop of tax-damned Ulyssia?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A holo-vid resolved in the middle of the board table. The image shook and blurred, steadied, then focused on the ornately dressed figure striding up the nave of St Hedges Cathedral. The High Elvis in full regalia\'97sequinned cape catching light, sunglasses deflecting stained-glass beams across the congregation in calculated bursts of blue and gold. The camera followed him to the dais where the Very Arch Business Bishop d\'92Molesto half-rose from his throne, frozen in the hazy glow.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Psychological warfare,\'94 Gerry muttered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The High Elvis bowed\'97a studied gesture that felt like mockery\'97then reached for the gilded staff traditionally reserved for ceremonial blessings.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The cathedral erupted: \'93Holy Momma! Holy Momma!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93This is where he crosses the line,\'94 Tourism remarked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>D\'92Molesto adjusted his robes, defeated. The recording ended with chants intensifying into thundering applause.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What we just witnessed,\'94 Dunhilton said quietly, \'93was a calculated attack on the dignity of our Airborne institutions. A hospitality clone dared to rival the vicar of capitalism itself and walked away with the crowd\'92s faith.\'94 His voice dropped. \'93Give me actionable solutions. Are we gods, or are we whittled to shadows?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The reminder of their fragile standing sent shivers through the directors.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Defence leaned forward, grateful for something to contribute. \'93Military strike on Clambake. Precision hover-copt assault, minimal collateral\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Economic blockade of the Ghetto,\'94 Foreign Commerce tried. \'93Cut off food shipments, power\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They\'92ve survived worse.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Moral Observance dabbed his lips. \'93Counter-propaganda. Remind them of the virtues of profit-based spirituality\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They\'92re already worshipping a pregnant woman.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Corrections: \'93Mass arrests. Round up the leadership\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And make martyrs? No.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The proposals died. The directors watched Dunhilton, recalibrating.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Heston,\'94 Dunhilton said softly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Director of Freedom looked up, swallowing hard.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93This situation began with PAPER\'92s failure. Smythe, Grubler, compromised operations, missing bodies.\'94 Dunhilton\'92s voice remained calm, which made it worse. \'93The Elvi formed a government under your watch. They crowned a king under your watch. They infiltrated St Hedges under your watch.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Your Serene Corporateness, the operation predates my\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton raised his voice. \'93The Director of Freedom has regrettably elected to resign.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What?\'94 Heston What\'92s-His-Face demanded. Everyone knew Defence has been required to write a resignation letter, and were expecting everything to be pinned on him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton didn\'92t miss a beat. \'93Police Commissioner Hardman will step in as acting Director of Freedom, as well as official Director of Elvi Rights.\'94 Dunhilton shot a gaze through his eyebrows down the table at the stricken ex-director \'93Oh, sorry, Millicent, you\'94re fired as of thirty minutes ago. Now get out. Both of you get out now, or you\'92ll both be hugging pillows.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As the two stricken, defrocked ex-cabinet members scurried out\'97Elvi Rights, in her haste, forsook her tablet\'97those remaining in the room made a ceremony of congratulating and backslapping Gerry while totems of startled prey inhabited them and gave them startled, doomed eyes. Moral Observance secured another pastry and gnawed at it nervously.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Gerry will assume oversight of PAPER operations effective immediately. Defence, you\'92ll report directly to me until I decide whether to keep you or let you hug a pillow.\'94 Dunhilton stood. \'93The rest of you: if you have nothing useful to contribute, we are adjourned.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As the directors filed out, Dunhilton\'92s voice stopped them. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'94Gerry. Stay.\'94
